---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site.js';
// NOTE: Draft. Mirrors the in-app Privacy Policy with beta-era updates
// (voice transcripts, essay content, AI subprocessors, Stripe). Pending the
// user's legal review before this is treated as final.
---

<BaseLayout
  path="/privacy/"
  title="Privacy Policy: Mascot AI"
  description="How Mascot AI collects, uses, and protects your data during the private beta."
>
  <article class="container-x max-w-3xl py-16 legal sm:py-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl">Privacy Policy (Beta)</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted"><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 28, 2026</p>

    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Mascot AI is committed to protecting your privacy and being transparent about how we collect,
      use, and protect your personal information. This policy explains our practices while the
      platform is in private beta.
    </p>

    <h2>What data we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account information:</strong> email address, name, password (stored hashed), and account type (student or parent).</li>
      <li><strong>Profile information:</strong> academic history (GPA, test scores, coursework), extracurricular activities, honors, hometown, graduation year, college preferences, and free-text responses about your goals and experiences.</li>
      <li><strong>Uploaded documents:</strong> transcripts and other files you choose to upload for parsing.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice conversations:</strong> audio from voice sessions with Mascot and the text transcripts generated from them.</li>
      <li><strong>Essay content:</strong> drafts you write and the feedback conversations you have about them.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> features used, pages visited, and time spent, to operate and improve the service.</li>
      <li><strong>Device information:</strong> browser type, device type, IP address, and operating system, for support and security.</li>
      <li><strong>Billing information:</strong> subscription status and payment metadata. Card details are handled by Stripe and are not stored on our servers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we collect this data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account creation and authentication:</strong> to create and maintain your account and verify your identity.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice counseling and profile building:</strong> to hold conversations, remember what you've discussed, and build your profile.</li>
      <li><strong>College matching:</strong> to analyze your profile and produce personalized university recommendations with explanations.</li>
      <li><strong>Essay assistance:</strong> to analyze drafts and provide coaching feedback.</li>
      <li><strong>Product improvement:</strong> to understand how the platform is used and improve it.</li>
      <li><strong>Communication:</strong> to send important updates about your account and the service.</li>
      <li><strong>Security:</strong> to protect against fraud, abuse, and unauthorized access.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Service providers and AI processing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal data. We share data only with providers that help us run the
      platform, and only as needed to deliver the service:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>MongoDB Atlas</strong>: database hosting and storage.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Cloud Platform</strong>: application hosting.</li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong>: subscription payments.</li>
      <li><strong>Anthropic (Claude)</strong>: AI processing for university matching, essay analysis, and transcript parsing.</li>
      <li><strong>Google (Gemini)</strong>: AI processing for real-time voice conversations. Google also handles optional "Sign in with Google" authentication.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong>: aggregate traffic and usage measurement for our public website.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      When you use AI features, your relevant content is processed by these third-party AI services
      under their own privacy terms. We do not use your data to train AI models, and we do not share
      personally identifiable information with third parties for their own purposes without your
      consent.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Our public website at mascot-ai.com uses Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors find
      and use the site: pages viewed, referring source, approximate location, device type, and
      similar aggregate measures. Google Analytics sets cookies in your browser to do this. We have
      turned off Google Signals, so this data is not linked to your Google account or used for ad
      personalization, and we have set the shortest practical data retention.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can block these cookies through your browser settings or with the Google Analytics
      opt-out browser add-on. The rest of the website works without them.
    </p>

    <h2>Data security</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Passwords are stored using secure hashing algorithms.</li>
      <li>Data is transmitted over HTTPS.</li>
      <li>Access to personal data is restricted to authorized personnel.</li>
      <li>We review and update our security practices regularly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data sharing</h2>
    <p><strong>We do not sell your personal data to third parties.</strong> We may share information only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>with your explicit consent;</li>
      <li>with the service providers listed above;</li>
      <li>when required by law or to protect our legal rights;</li>
      <li>in connection with a business transfer such as a merger or acquisition.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If parent linking is enabled for your account, a parent you approve can be granted read-only
      access to parts of your profile, matches, and essays. You control which sections are shared.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access:</strong> view and export your profile information from your account settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction:</strong> update your information at any time in your account.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> request deletion of your account and associated data by contacting us.</li>
      <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> request a copy of your data in a machine-readable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt-out:</strong> opt out of certain data collection and communications.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your personal information for as long as your account is active or as needed to
      provide the service. Deleted content is first marked inactive and then removed. If you request
      account deletion, we delete your personal information within 30 days, except where we are
      required to retain it for legal or regulatory purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Mascot AI is intended for students aged 13 and older, and for parents assisting students. For
      users under 18 we require parental or guardian consent, and for users under 13 we require
      verifiable parental consent before an account is activated. If you believe we have collected
      information from a child without the required consent, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Paid subscriptions are processed by Stripe. We receive subscription status and limited billing
      metadata, and we do not receive or store full card numbers.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Beta notice:</strong> Mascot AI is in private beta. Features, data retention policies,
      and service availability may change. We recommend not submitting highly sensitive personal
      information during the beta period, and we will notify users of significant changes to these
      practices.
    </div>

    <h2>International users</h2>
    <p>
      If you access the service from outside the United States, your information may be transferred
      to, stored, and processed in the United States. By using the service, you consent to this
      transfer.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the updated policy on this page and
      change the "Last updated" date, and we will notify users of material changes.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      For questions or requests about this policy or your data, including account deletion, data
      access or portability, privacy complaints, and GDPR or CCPA requests, contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We respond to all requests within a
      reasonable time, usually within 30 days.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
